{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CftKUiU2BRiT3XmAdFDQV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**I'd recommend building now, keeping the first release small, and measuring the effect as it rolls out.** A separate research phase would cost more than it would tell you.\n\n**Why build now**\n- **Customers already pay for this.** 14 of your 120 clinics (12%) buy a separate SMS tool and upload a CSV every night to feed it. That's clear demand, and a built-in version could replace that tool.\n- **The pilot fits what's widely reported.** Appointment reminders reducing no-shows is well documented in healthcare. Your 19%→11% drop, against 18% in the comparison clinics, points the same way.\n- **Being wrong costs little.** Basic SMS reminders through an existing SMS provider such as Twilio are a modest build. Three engineers for six weeks is plenty for a first version.\n\n**Why the pilot doesn't settle the size of the effect**\n- It's only 3 vs 3 clinics over 4 weeks, and the pilot clinics volunteered, so they may be unusually motivated.\n- Messages sent by hand may work better than automated ones, and some of the effect may fade as the novelty wears off.\n- So plan on a meaningful reduction, but don't promise 8 points.\n\n**What to resolve before or during the build**\n1. **Patient consent and opt-out** under the laws that apply to you, such as TCPA in the US or GDPR/PECR in the UK and EU.\n2. **Data quality.** Check how many bookings have a valid mobile number.\n3. **Pricing.** Decide whether SMS is included, sold as an add-on, or charged per message, since message costs grow with volume.\n\n**Suggested plan**\n- **Weeks 1–4:** one reminder 24–48 hours before the appointment, opt-out handling, delivery tracking, and settings for each clinic.\n- **Weeks 5–6:** turn it on in waves of clinics, starting with the 14 that already pay for SMS. Use the clinics not yet switched on as a comparison group to measure the real effect.\n- **Later:** two-way replies to confirm or cancel, and offering freed slots to waitlisted patients, once the data supports them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3193,"cache_read_input_tokens":5086,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3193},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b9debfb7-7cfd-4586-9488-9669bd5416b8","uuid":"436ec51e-c925-46c9-94f9-e49874efff13","timestamp":"2026-10-10T09:28:14.797Z","request_id":"req_011CftKUiEPJtEANkJ8FzYpi"}
